<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Elsevier wants to control Open Data</title>
<script type="text/javascript" id="MathJax-script" async
  src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js">
</script>
<style>
  body {
    font-family: 'Segoe UI', Arial, sans-serif;
    background: #fff;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 30px 40px;
  }

  h1 {
    text-align: center;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 42px;
    margin: 0 0 30px 0;
    color: #111;
  }

  .row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 15px;
  }

  .left-col {
    width: 45%;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .right-col {
    width: 52%;
  }

  .intro-text {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: #222;
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .intro-text a {
    color: #1155cc;
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .quote-block {
    position: relative;
    background: #e9e9e9;
    padding: 15px 20px 15px 25px;
    border-left: 6px solid #7a1f2b;
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: #111;
  }

  .attribution {
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 18px;
    color: #333;
    margin-top: 10px;
    margin-left: 60px;
  }

  .placeholder {
    width: 100%;
    height: 340px;
    background: repeating-linear-gradient(
      45deg, #ccc, #ccc 10px, #ddd 10px, #ddd 20px
    );
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    color: #555;
    font-size: 15px;
    text-align: center;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    border: 1px solid #999;
  }

  .img-caption {
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: #222;
    margin-top: 6px;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .and-label {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: #111;
    margin: 25px 0 8px 0;
  }

  .quote-block.highlight {
    background: #e9e9e9;
    border-left: 6px solid #7a1f2b;
    border: 3px solid red;
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: #111;
    padding: 15px 20px;
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

  <h1>Elsevier wants to control Open Data</h1>

  <div class="row">
    <div class="left-col">
      <div class="intro-text">
        Speaking on the 28th of April 2014 the Vice Chancellor of Cambridge University,
        <a href="#">Leszek Borysiewicz</a>, commented on the amount the university is paying to publisher Elsevier. He said:
      </div>

      <div class="quote-block">
        Yes we spend money with Elsevier. Do I regret spending money with Elsevier? By and large yes I do because I think they&rsquo;re rich enough already.
      </div>
      <div class="attribution">[asked by Michelle Brook]</div>
    </div>

    <div class="right-col">
      <div class="placeholder">
        [Photo/Video still: Cambridge University Vice Chancellor Leszek Borysiewicz seated in a chair, arms crossed, in front of window blinds]
      </div>
      <div class="img-caption">
        Cambridge University Vice Chancellor Leszek Borysiewicz at Q&amp;A Session on 28 April 2014
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="and-label">and:</div>

  <div class="quote-block highlight">
    just wait until we get into open data debates &hellip; Elsevier is already looking at ways in which it can control open data as a private company rather than the public bodies concerned.
  </div>

</body>
